  "changelog_html": "<h4>0.4.0</h4>\n<p>Updates now install by themselves. Turn this off any time from the Plugins screen.</p>\n<h4>0.3.7</h4>\n<p>Store Chat can answer questions about the product a shopper is viewing, including its description and stock status.</p>\n<h4>0.3.6</h4>\n<p>Store check shows where the Try-On button sits and whether product details were found. Only daily counts are sent, with no visitor data.</p>\n<h4>0.3.5</h4>\n<p>Try-On limits each visitor fairly, including stores behind a proxy. Stores using a public proxy can select its trusted address header in WooCommerce settings.</p>\n<h4>0.3.4</h4>\n<p>The Try it on button on product pages shows the animated try-on icon, in the gradient and size set in the GRINDCTRL dashboard, from the first page load.</p>\n<h4>0.3.3</h4>\n<p>Try it on buttons on product listings follow the card pill switch in the GRINDCTRL dashboard, and hide when Try-On is switched off there.</p>\n<h4>0.3.2</h4>\n<p>Try-On uses an existing image derivative near 1024 pixels when available, reducing garment downloads.</p>\n<p>Merchant preview links carry their test-look token through the Try-On context request.</p>\n<h4>0.3.1</h4>\n<p>Try-On size picker on WooCommerce: variations are offered in the Try-On sheet and the chosen one is added to the cart.</p>\n<p>Order status works on sites with plain permalinks, and finds orders by the number a sequential-order-number plugin shows.</p>\n<p>Try it on pills also appear on Product Collection block cards.</p>\n<p>Stronger replay protection for signed order requests.</p>\n<h4>0.3.0</h4>\n<p>Order status and tracking in chat, with logged-in shoppers recognised automatically.</p>\n<p>AI Virtual Try-On: product-page button, listing pills, shortcode and block, with add to cart from the result.</p>\n<p>Personal data exporter and eraser for GRINDCTRL chats; deleting the plugin schedules this site&#39;s GRINDCTRL data for deletion after 48 hours.</p>\n<h4>0.2.0</h4>\n<p>Connect the site with a one-time connection code from the GRINDCTRL dashboard.</p>\n<p>Signed daily check-in so the dashboard shows the plugin version and when it was last seen.</p>\n<p>Disconnect button. Deactivating or deleting the plugin tells GRINDCTRL the site is disconnected.</p>\n<p>The manual embed key moved under Advanced.</p>\n<h4>0.1.0</h4>\n<p>First version: settings page, chat loader, WooCommerce product and cart context.</p>"
